id: ops-release-npm-runtime
title: Release and CI install Dependabot locks with the same pinned npm
description: Daily Release run 42412827958 failed before publishing because trusted tool and audit installs used npm 10.9.3 from Node 22.18.0 against the 091124b lock. Standardize release and CI on exact npm 11.21.0 before any locked install.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-ops#260"
created_at: "2026-11-07T23:40:56.448Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-08T04:08:56.313Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Inventory every workflow and script npm install with before and after runtimes; Pin and verify npm before trusted tool, provenance and caller installs while retaining node-version and ignore-scripts; PR CI executes the exact release production install against both committed locks; Document passing fixed and failing npm 10.9.3 runs against the unchanged 091124b fixture; Focused tests and typecheck pass; CI is the full gate; docs explain the caller runtime"
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T23:40:58.995Z",pi-agent,"Repro: on main 091124b (Dependabot #254), npm 10.9.3 ci --omit=dev --ignore-scripts --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund reports EUSAGE: glob@13.0.6 does not satisfy glob@13.0.7. Reported npm 11.17.0 succeeds. CI already selects 11.21.0; release selects 11.19.0 only after tool bootstrap, while audit/alert/recover/Bun hooks inherit bundled npm. Plan: pin packageManager to 11.21.0, install and verify it immediately after setup-node in all reusable jobs, add isolated exact-command root/private PR CI smoke checks, retain lock bytes and lifecycle suppression."
  "2026-11-07T23:44:59.543Z",pi-agent,"Revert proof: immutable 091124b package.json/package-lock.json fixtures on real Node 22.18.0: exact npm ci --omit=dev --ignore-scripts --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund exits 1 with npm 10.9.3 (EUSAGE; glob@13.0.6 does not satisfy glob@13.0.7), exits 0 with npm 11.21.0 (5 production packages). Private provenance fixture passes with both npm versions (52 packages). All four runs preserve the lock SHA-256. In a disposable source copy, retaining new tests/manifests but restoring only both workflows to 091124b gives 0/3 pass and 3 failures; restoring fixed workflows gives 3/3 pass, no skips. Original worktree is never reverted. npm 11.21.0 engine range ^20.17.0 || >=22.9.0 admits the Node 22.18.0 default."
  "2026-11-07T23:45:00.919Z",pi-agent,"Local gates: focused workflow/runtime tests 43/43 pass, zero failures/skips; npm run typecheck and npm run build:test pass; lint passes; duplication 0% (0/37768 lines, 141 sources, zero clones); docstring 48 files/370 declarations pass. Full npm/Bun release gates and Windows consumers are delegated to PR CI per task scope. docs/reusable-release.md contains the complete before/after install inventory. Both committed locks remain byte-identical to 091124b. No release dispatch, publication or merge performed."
  "2026-11-07T23:46:03.257Z",pi-agent,The new CI lock-smoke shell step also ran unchanged locally under pinned npm 11.21.0 against fresh copies of the current root and private manifests/locks; both installations succeeded. PM linked-test execution uses the default sandbox context; no test-run artifacts are written into the package tracker.
  "2026-11-07T23:51:01.184Z",pi-agent,"PR #260 is ready for review. Initial CI run 42426776935: both new lock compatibility jobs passed (Node 22.18.0 and 26); Windows Node 22 and CodeQL passed. Full Node 26 npm gate found one additional older structural assertion in test/release-continuation-adapter.test.ts that prohibited even the now-required global npm bootstrap (1632 passed, 1 failed, 2 platform skips). Updated that assertion to require the exact pinned script-disabled npm bootstrap and retain the prohibition on all other reconciliation npm installs. Expanding focused coverage to include the adapter suite; fresh exact-head CI will verify the follow-up."
  "2026-11-07T23:52:06.683Z",pi-agent,"Follow-up local verification passes: adapter suite 62/62 with zero failures/skips (via linked pm test), bringing focused coverage to 105 passing tests including the original 43 workflow/runtime tests. Test compilation and typecheck pass after the assertion update. Reconciliation still forbids project npm installs, while requiring the exact verified npm bootstrap. Initial CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/42426776935 completed with 4 successful jobs (both lock gates and both Windows consumers) and the 2 Linux test jobs failing only the old adapter assertion. CodeQL passed separately. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/260 will receive fresh exact-head gates; no old-head success is treated as final verification."
  "2026-11-08T00:01:44.834Z",pi-agent,"CI at 66a3a1a: both Linux suites pass 1633 tests with 2 platform skips each and 100% coverage thresholds across 48 measured sources. Both npm gates then refuse the new PowerShell $LASTEXITCODE conditional in ci.yml as an unresolved publish path. Use explicit Bash for Windows npm setup instead, retaining the selected Node global prefix, set -euo pipefail and exact active-version check. npm run verify:release-publish-attestation now passes locally; all three pin/lock regressions pass; typecheck passes. Parser follow-up ops-attestation-powershell-guards tracks the out-of-scope shell-language issue. Windows consumers, lock gates and CodeQL all passed at 66a3a1a; final CI must run again after this change."
  "2026-11-08T03:03:57.816Z",codex-sol,"Re-review class audit: (1) metadata-only recovery must not depend on registry installation; defer reconciliation npm bootstrap into the locked-runtime installer. (2) failure reporting must survive bootstrap and dependency-install failures; attempt the configured alert even when setup fails, without installing locks with bundled npm. (3) bootstrap exceptions must allow exactly one pinned npm install and inspect every command. (4) runtime failure tests must enumerate every reusable and CI setup, including Windows. Searched workflows, scripts, templates, SDK/CLI, JSON/TOON and packed/no-git consumers: the changed paths are release infrastructure; tracker/output contracts remain unaffected. Reusing PR #260 and this item; origin/main is already an ancestor."
  "2026-11-08T03:07:55.575Z",codex-sol,"Revert proof in disposable source copies: restoring only the prior workflow fails the reconciliation/alert assertions; restoring only release-runtime.ts fails the on-demand installer regression. Across all 7 eager reusable setups and all 3 CI setups (including Windows), appended unrelated global installs, removed exact-version guards and swallowed bootstrap failures are detected in 30/30 mutations. Fixed baseline and restored fixed copies pass. Both reconciliation test files inspect all steps without exemptions. The native empty probe still invokes no npm; both on-demand private and trusted-tool installers reject stale/newer npm and install failures before ci. Focused direct run: 107/107 pass, no skips; test compilation passes."
  "2026-11-08T03:26:59.631Z",codex-sol,"Expanded focused linked test run passes 112/112 with zero skips, including both real npm lifecycle/consumer tests and the fixture-precondition suite. First full gate measured all four coverage dimensions at 100% across 48 sources but reported three test failures: a newly introduced literal-name filter violated the existing fixture guard, and the npx bootstrap launcher propagated ignore-scripts into two lifecycle tests. Replaced the selector with one explicit expected name plus an exact per-job cardinality assertion; no existing guard or test was weakened. Full gates now run the cached pinned npm binary directly, without bootstrap-only config leaking into the suite, under isolated Git configuration."
  "2026-11-08T03:44:14.827Z",codex-sol,"Additional class instances found during the package-wide audit: request invokes only Node/GitHub commands and direct HTTP OIDC preflight, so its global npm bootstrap is unnecessary; verify_bun invokes npm only for a configured bunx hook. Removed request bootstrap and guarded Bun bootstrap with the same caller-hook condition as its locked install. Reconciliation/request tests prohibit installation commands in every metadata-only step, and all remaining reusable plus CI setup bodies retain exact-command and four-outcome checks. Interrupted the old Bun gate so final evidence will cover this broader fix; the prior npm gate passed 1635 tests with 2 platform skips, 100% all four dimensions across 48 sources, and all remaining release checks. A separate reused-checkout strict health check reports environment-specific extension-host skew and driver drift; no driver or dependency changes are authorized by this task, and fresh-checkout CI will verify health."
  "2026-11-08T04:08:55.191Z",codex-sol,"Final class fix verified: metadata-only reconcile/request jobs perform no eager npm installation; reconciliation pins npm 11.21.0 only before a missing locked runtime install; Bun bootstrap is conditional on its caller hook; alert scripts are attempted after bootstrap or dependency-install failure, with locked installs allowed only after verified setup. Exact bootstrap-command checks inspect every command in all 6 remaining reusable and 3 CI setups. Final disposable proofs catch 27 bootstrap mutations (extra install, wrong version, swallowed failure), 2 metadata-install mutations and 1 unconditional Bun-bootstrap mutation; both workflow-only and runtime-only reversions also fail, and restored fixed sources pass. Linked focused command passes 112/112, zero skips. On Node 26.13.0 with npm 11.21.0 and isolated Git configuration, npm run release:check and bun run release:check both pass: 1635 passed, 0 failed, 2 platform skips each; 100% statements/branches/functions/lines across all 48 measured sources, 0% duplication, 371 documented declarations, zero root/private audit vulnerabilities, and all changelog/attestation/lifecycle gates pass. Both locks remain unchanged from 091124b; original real npm 10.9.3 EUSAGE versus npm 11.21.0 lock proof is retained above. PR #260 remains the sole PR. Fresh-checkout CI and automated re-review follow the push; no release, publication or merge was performed. The separate reused-checkout strict-health environment warnings remain documented above."
